{"step_index":137,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-15T21:57:54Z","content":"> [!WARNING] Token Permission Denied\n> `remote: Permission to pp0016/PRIYANSHU-README.git denied to pp0016.`\n\nI successfully applied your token, and GitHub recognized you as `pp0016`! However, it still blocked the push. \n\nBecause your token starts with `github_pat_`, it is a **Fine-Grained Personal Access Token**. When you created it, it looks like it wasn't given permission to write code to this repository.\n\n**To fix this:**\n1. Go back to GitHub where you created the token.\n2. Ensure you have given it access to the `PRIYANSHU-README` repository.\n3. Under **Repository permissions**, make sure **\"Contents\"** is set to **\"Read and write\"**. \n\nOnce you update the token's permissions on GitHub, you don't even need to give me a new token. Just tell me when it's updated, and I will try the push again!","thinking":"**Prioritizing Tool Selection**\n\nI'm now zeroing in on the importance of tool selection. My focus is crystal clear: using the most relevant and precise tool for any given task. To that end, I'll meticulously list all potentially relevant tools before making any calls, with an emphasis on choosing the most specific option available.\n\n\n"}
