{"step_index":201,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-15T22:25:27Z","thinking":"**Prioritizing Tool Selection**\n\nI'm now zeroing in on the importance of tool selection. My focus is sharpened; I must identify the most precise tool for each individual task to optimize performance. I've begun to list out related tools to clarify options and facilitate efficient selection. Specificity is key; I'll always prefer `view_file`, `write_to_file`, or `replace_file` when applicable.\n\n\n**Refining Transcript Processing**\n\nI've shifted gears toward a more efficient method. The 60+ transcript files are overwhelming, so I'll create a Python script, at `/work/backfill_script.py`, to parse them. It will extract and consolidate user queries from each `.jsonl` file into a comprehensive `backfilled_chats_summary.md` document for the user, rather than analyzing each file individually. This is a more agentic and manageable approach.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"CodeContent":"\"import os\\nimport json\\nimport glob\\nfrom datetime import datetime\\n\\nbrain_dir = r\\\"C:\\\\Users\\\\renu5\\\\.gemini\\\\antigravity\\\\brain\\\"\\noutput_file = r\\\"c:\\\\Users\\\\renu5\\\\Downloads\\\\priyanshu readme\\\\work\\\\backfilled_chats_summary.md\\\"\\n\\ndef extract_chats():\\n    with open(output_file, 'w', encoding='utf-8') as out:\\n        out.write(\\\"# Backfilled Chat History\\\\n\\\\n\\\")\\n        out.write(\\\"This file contains the extracted history from all other chat sessions related to `priyanshu readme`.\\\\n\\\\n\\\")\\n        \\n        folders = glob.glob(os.path.join(brain_dir, \\\"*\\\", \\\".system_generated\\\", \\\"logs\\\", \\\"transcript.jsonl\\\"))\\n        \\n        relevant_chats = []\\n        for path in folders:\\n            is_relevant = False\\n            try:\\n                with open(path, 'r', encoding='utf-8') as f:\\n                    content = f.read()\\n                    if \\\"priyanshu readme\\\" in content.lower() or \\\"stickman\\\" in content.lower():\\n                        is_relevant = True\\n            except:\\n                continue\\n                \\n            if not is_relevant:\\n                continue\\n                \\n            # If relevant, parse it\\n            out.write(f\\\"## Session: {os.path.basename(os.path.dirname(os.path.dirname(os.path.dirname(path))))}\\\\n\\\")\\n            \\n            try:\\n                with open(path, 'r', encoding='utf-8') as f:\\n                    for line in f:\\n                        data = json.loads(line)\\n                        if data.get('type') == 'USER_INPUT':\\n                            time = data.get('created_at', 'Unknown time')\\n                            text = data.get('content', '')\\n                            out.write(f\\\"**[{time}] USER:** {text[:500]}...\\\\n\\\\n\\\")\\n            except Exception as e:\\n                out.write(f\\\"Error parsing: {str(e)}\\\\n\\\\n\\\")\\n                \\n            out.write(\\\"---\\\\n\\\\n\\\")\\n            \\n    print(f\\\"Extraction complete! Saved to {output_file}\\\")\\n\\nif __name__ == \\\"__main__\\\":\\n    extract_chats()\\n\"","Description":"\"Created script to extract all past chat history from brain.\"","Overwrite":"false","TargetFile":"\"c:/Users/renu5/Downloads/priyanshu readme/work/backfill_script.py\"","toolAction":"\"Writing to file\"","toolSummary":"\"Create backfill script\""}}]}
